\subsection{Runtime}\label{sec:runtime}

Table~\ref{tab:runtime} and Fig.~\ref{fig:runtime}. Denoising a $552\times990$ B-scan takes \PROP_TIME~s; the
one-off dictionary build costs \TRAIN_SEC~s and is amortised over every image processed afterwards. SRAD's
per-image learning costs \SRAD_TIME~s on the same machine, giving the \SPEEDUP$\times$ factor reported in
Section~\ref{sec:real} (the paper reports $\approx6\times$; the difference is explained by our smaller images and by
the SRAD dictionary being learned on 15\,000 patches against the global one's 30\,000).

